# Thought Reflection (Bot1's) and Notion Thief (Bot2's) both replace Bot1's draws outside its draw step: Bot1, the drawing
# player, chooses which applies first (CR 616.1; both cards' rulings). In its turn 3 draw step the first draw is exempt from
# Notion Thief, so only Thought Reflection replaces it; of the two cards it draws instead, the first is still the first
# Bot1 draws in the draw step and is drawn, and Notion Thief replaces the second - Bot2 draws it. Then Bot1 casts Ancestral
# Recall and has Notion Thief apply first to each draw: Bot1 skips it and Bot2 draws one card, and Thought Reflection has
# no draw of Bot1's left to replace (CR 614.6), nor is Bot2's draw one of Bot1's. Bot1 ends with no cards in hand and Bot2
# draws three for the three draws (six with Thought Reflection first, as the scenario beside this one shows).

